---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Compare from "../components/Compare.astro";
import { neighbors } from "../lib/nav";
const { prev, next } = neighbors("overloads");
---

<Base title="25. Overloads, optional & params — C# vs TypeScript" description="25. Overloads, optional & params: side-by-side C# and TypeScript examples." slug="overloads">
  <div slot="header" id="top">
    <p><small><a href="/">C# vs TS</a> / 25. Overloads, optional & params</small></p>
    <h1>25. Overloads, optional &amp; params</h1>
    <p><strong>How to read:</strong> left is C#, middle is TypeScript, right is blank Mystery (yours). Narrow screens stack.</p>
  </div>

  <section id="overloads">
  
  <h2>25. Overloads, optional &amp; params</h2>
  <Compare>
    <div slot="left">
      <pre><code>string Format(int n) =&gt; n.ToString();
string Format(double n, int digits = 2) =&gt; n.ToString($"F&#123;digits&#125;");

int Sum(params int[] nums) =&gt; nums.Sum();
Sum(1, 2, 3);
Sum(new[] &#123; 1, 2 &#125;);</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div slot="right">
      <pre><code>function format(n: number): string;
function format(n: number, digits: number): string;
function format(n: number, digits = 0): string &#123;
  return n.toFixed(digits);
&#125;

function sum(...nums: number[]): number &#123;
  return nums.reduce((a, b) =&gt; a + b, 0);
&#125;
sum(1, 2, 3); sum(...[1, 2]);</code></pre>
    </div>
  </Compare>
  <ul>
    <li>C# resolves overloads by arity/types at compile time. TS overloads are compile-time only — one runtime implementation handles all.</li>
    <li><code>params int[]</code> ≈ <code>...nums: number[]</code>. Spread <code>...</code> works at call sites and in literals in TS.</li>
  </ul>

  </section>

  <nav class="pager" aria-label="Previous / next topic">
    <span>{prev ? <a href={`/${prev.slug}/`}>← {prev.title}</a> : <span />}</span>
    <span><a href="/">All topics</a></span>
    <span>{next ? <a href={`/${next.slug}/`}>{next.title} →</a> : <span />}</span>
  </nav>
</Base>
